{{!-- add-chantry-inventory-effects-and-roster (task 3.6) — one construction Trait's ROSTER.

      `traits.allies ●●` says there are two allies and does not say WHO. This is where the who goes:
      per-entry name, note and the points that entry consumes, summed against the Trait's own
      circles.

      VALIDATED BY POINTS, NOT BY ROW COUNT (design.md D5). "Aliados — 2 puntos por punto — Un
      consorte, Ciudadano Extraordinario, espíritu, EDE, u otro aliado excepcional POR PUNTO" reads
      one-to-one for Aliados, but Biblioteca and Nodo do not count heads and Ancianos has grades of
      power. So each entry declares the points it consumes (1 by default, 0 allowed) and the rule is
      Σ points ≤ circles. Aliados ●● therefore takes two one-point allies OR one exceptional
      two-point ally, and Biblioteca ●●● takes five descriptive 0-point entries without breaking.

      Only the EIGHT Traits that are collections get one (`ROSTER_TRAIT_KEYS` in
      `module/scripts/chantry-effects.js`). The rest are magnitudes: `resources` is money,
      `arcane-cloaking` is a penalty, `reality-zone`/`enhancement`/`requisitions` are ceilings, and
      `integrated-effects` has its own point table on its own tab.

      WHEN THIS RENDERS AT ALL: `roster.show`, computed in `_prepareContext`, is true when the roster
      HAS entries or the sheet is unlocked. A locked sheet with an empty roster renders nothing here,
      which is what keeps the spec's promise that "an empty roster SHALL NOT change how an existing
      sheet reads" literally true, while an unlocked sheet still offers the way to add the first one.

      CONTEXT DEPTH. `locked` is passed in as a hash argument, so inside the `{{#each}}` below it is
      `../locked` — one level up from the array element, exactly as `item_table.hbs` does it. This is
      the trap that has already shipped twice on this system's mage partials (a bare `locked` inside
      an `{{#each}}` resolves against the ARRAY ELEMENT, so `(eq locked false)` is false and the
      control never renders, not even unlocked), and the depth used here was established by PROBING
      THE RENDERED HTML — `.github/scripts/test-chantry-sheet-render.mjs` renders this partial in
      both lock states and counts the write controls, and fails if the locked count is not zero or
      the unlocked count is not more than zero.

      ARGUMENTS (all required from the caller):
        - `roster`   — `{ show, entries, used, allowed, over }` for ONE Trait
        - `traitkey` — that Trait's key, carried on every control so the handler knows what to write
        - `locked`   — the sheet's lock state --}}
<div class="chantry-roster" data-key="{{traitkey}}">

	<div class="chantry-roster-head">
		<span class="chantry-roster-total {{#if roster.over}}item-warning{{/if}}"
				title="{{#if roster.over}}{{localize 'wod.chantry.roster.over'}}{{else}}{{localize 'wod.chantry.roster.points'}}{{/if}}">
			{{localize "wod.chantry.roster.points"}}: {{roster.used}} / {{roster.allowed}}
		</span>

		{{#if (eq locked false)}}
			<button type="button" class="v3-iconbtn chantry-roster-add" data-action="rosterAdd" data-key="{{traitkey}}"
					title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.roster.add'}}">
				<i class="icon fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
				<span class="v3-sr-only">{{localize "wod.chantry.roster.add"}}</span>
			</button>
		{{/if}}
	</div>

	{{#each roster.entries as |entry index|}}
		<div class="chantry-roster-row" data-key="{{../traitkey}}" data-index="{{index}}">

			{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
				<input class="inputdata editable chantry-roster-name" type="text" value="{{entry.name}}"
						data-source="roster" data-field="name" data-key="{{../traitkey}}" data-index="{{index}}"
						placeholder="{{localize 'wod.chantry.roster.name'}}" autocomplete="off" />
				<input class="inputdata editable chantry-roster-note" type="text" value="{{entry.note}}"
						data-source="roster" data-field="note" data-key="{{../traitkey}}" data-index="{{index}}"
						placeholder="{{localize 'wod.chantry.roster.note'}}" autocomplete="off" />
				<input class="inputdata editable chantry-roster-points" type="number" min="0" value="{{entry.points}}"
						data-source="roster" data-field="points" data-key="{{../traitkey}}" data-index="{{index}}"
						title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.roster.entrypoints'}}" />
				<a class="pointer item-delete chantry-roster-delete" data-action="rosterDelete"
						data-key="{{../traitkey}}" data-index="{{index}}"
						title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.roster.remove'}}"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-trash-can" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
			{{else}}
				{{!-- Locked: plain text, never a disabled control — the same choice the Tipo/Nivel
				      rows on the Rasgos tab already make (existing requirement, "SHALL render as
				      text, not a disabled control, when locked"). --}}
				<span class="chantry-roster-name">{{entry.name}}</span>
				<span class="chantry-roster-note">{{entry.note}}</span>
				<span class="chantry-roster-points">{{entry.points}}</span>
			{{/if}}

		</div>
	{{/each}}

</div>
